  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Fiji, P4SP worked with the Ministry for Women, Children and Social Protection (MWCSP) to strengthened monitoring and evaluation capacity within the Ministry. Through training and workshops, P4SP helped MWCSP to establish an evidence-based approach to assessing the impact of the government&#x2019;s social welfare programs. P4SP also led the operational design of the grievance and redress mechanism for all social assistance schemes. This was incorporated within each schemes&#x2019; Standard Operating Procedures and endorsed by MWCSP&#x2019;s leadership. 
&#x200d;
In Kiribati, P4SP&#x2019;s long-term technical adviser supported the Ministry for Women, Youth, Sports and Social Affairs (MWYSSA) to deliver more robust strategic and operational planning and improve communications with citizens.  P4SP continued strengthening implementation of the Support Fund for the Unemployed and the Senior Citizens Allowance by improving case management tracking and monitoring processes and designing training to support the rollout of the program&#x2019;s operations manuals. 
&#x200d;
During the reporting period, P4SP&#x2019;s support to Tonga enabled the strengthening of locally identified solutions to reducing exclusion risks, such as home delivery of payments to elderly benefit beneficiaries who are unable to collect their payments and support for extending services to remote, outer islands.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social protection measures</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati&#x2019;s latest Household Income and Expenditure (HIES) survey (data from 2023-24) saw a significant reduction in the national poverty rate from 21.9% of the population in 2019-20 to 5.5% in 2023-24, meaning 19,000 i-Kiribati have been lifted out of poverty over that period. The HIES report attributes Kiribati&#x2019;s Support Fund for the Unemployed (SFU) as the main driver of this reduction in poverty. Nearly 95% of the population in 2023&#x2013;2024 lived in a household with at least one SFU recipient. P4SP provided Kiribati&#x2019;s Ministry for Women, Youth, Sports and Social Affairs (MWYSSA) with assistance to enhance delivery of the SFU and other social assistance programs. 
&#x200d;
In Fiji, P4SP finalised the standard operating procedures for the Ministry of Women, Children and Social Protection (MWCSP) to deliver Fiji&#x2019;s six social protection schemes, with a focus on improving payment procedures. 
&#x200d;
In Tonga, P4SP provided modelling and advice to government which informed (further) social protection reforms incorporated into the 2025 budget. P4SP also strengthened the implementation of the Social Welfare Scheme for the Elderly through an operations review and development of guidelines and standard operating procedures.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">P4SP expanded its partnership work during this reporting period, working with seven (7) Organisations of Persons with Disabilities (OPDs) in the reporting period - 2 in Tonga,1 in Kiribati, 1 in Vanuatu (new) and 1 in the Solomon Islands (new), and 2 regional organisations.
&#x200d;
In Kiribati, P4SP&#x2019;s partnership with Te Toa Matoa was instrumental in finalising the Disability Support Allowance (DSA) Review which commenced in 2023/24. This engagement with Te Toa Matoa ensured the lived experience of people with disabilities was reflected in the review findings and recommendations to improve the accessibility and adequacy of the scheme. 
&#x200d;
Working through established relationships with the Pacific Disability Forum and Pacific Leprosy Association, P4SP partnered with national OPDs Lavame&#x2019;a Ta&#x2019;e&#x2019;iloa Disabled People Association Incorporated (LATA) and Naunau &#x2018;o e &#x2018;Alamaite Tonga Association (NATA) in Tonga, People with Disabilities Solomon Islands, the Vanuatu Society for People with Disabilities to inform operational and policy reform work on disability benefit adequacy.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social protection measures</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">P4SP has supported government agencies in the Pacific to strengthen social protection programs.  In Fiji P4SP is supporting the Ministry for Women, Children and Social Protection to deliver Fiji&#x2019;s six social protection schemes by updating Standard Operating Procedures and building a Management Information System for all six schemes, which benefit 146,566 people including 12,572 people with disabilities. P4SP also supported a major reform to the Bus Fare Concession Scheme in Fiji making it more inclusive for persons with disabilities and those living in remote and maritime areas. In Kiribati P4SP has supported MWYSSA to develop an Operations Manual for the Support Fund for the Unemployed and Senior Citizens Allowance and train staff on its implementation, contributing to more efficient delivery of these social protection schemes which benefit 62,301 people.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">P4SP has worked directly with 7 Organisations of Persons with Disabilities (OPDs) in the reporting period (4 in Tonga,1 in Kiribati and 2 regional organisations).  In Tonga P4SP provided a short training to government and non-government stakeholders (24 participants) to develop a shared understanding of the importance of, and opportunities for improving disability-inclusive social protection in Tonga.  The training was for OPDs and non-OPDs. Representatives from 4 OPDs attended and 25% of all participants (6 people) reported being people living with a disability.  All OPDs were Tongan organisations.  P4SP&#x2019;s support to the Ministry of Women, Youth, Sport and Social Affairs (MWYSSA) in Kiribati included undertaking a detailed review of the Disability Support Allowance (DSA). Te Toa Matoa (TTM), a national OPD has engaged closely with P4SP on this work and the Pacific Disability Forum and Pacific Leprosy Association were also consulted.</narrative>
    </description>
