    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnerships for Social Protection in the Pacific and Timor Leste (P4SP) worked with governments to strengthen social protection delivery systems by undertaking operational reviews of social protection schemes and then supporting governments to strengthen them through the development of Operations Manuals and Management Information Systems. In addition, in Fiji, P4SP has supported a major reform to the Bus Fare Concession Scheme in Fiji making it more inclusive for persons with disabilities and those living in remote and maritime areas. In Kiribati, P4SP&#x2019;s deployed adviser acts as Director of the Social Protection Unit in MWYSSA and has worked to establish this unit and strengthen its capacity to effectively deliver social protection in Kiribati. In Tonga, P4SP provided modelling and advice to government which was incorporated into the 2024 budget and will see significant reforms to the Social Welfare Scheme (elderly benefit) from 2024 onwards, including lowering the age of eligibility.</narrative>
